<task id="to_create_an_online_lookup_f7f69e" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>To create an online lookup</title>
   <shortdesc>A Search and Select Action on the object that corresponds to the lookup value field</shortdesc>
   <prolog>
      <author type="creator">Rakesh Singh</author>
       <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>lookup</keyword>
        <keyword>Select</keyword>
        <keyword>click</keyword>
        <keyword>Search</keyword>
        <keyword>field</keyword>
        <keyword>Display</keyword>
        <indexterm>lookup</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Select</indexterm>
        <indexterm>click</indexterm>
      </keywords>
          <prodinfo>
        <prodname/>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <taskbody>
      <context>
         <p> A Search and Select Action on the object that corresponds to the lookup value field must exist. For example, if you need an account lookup, there must be a Search and Select Action on the Account object.</p>
      </context>
      <steps>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click <b>Display Map</b>. </cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Select a Display Map and click <b>Edit</b>. The Display Map panel opens.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>In the Mapped Details section of the Display Map pane, click the magnify icon  to open lookup properties for that field.</cmd>
            <info>
               <image href="../attachments/98667726/98668079.jpg" width="21" height="23" placement="inline">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Select <b>Search And Select (Online)</b>.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Select the applicable Search and Select Actions.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>In the <b>Mapped Record ID</b> field, select the record ID field and click <b>Save</b>.This ensures that the correct lookup will be returned to the record. To remove an existing Online Lookup, click <b>Remove</b>.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98668077</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667726/98668077.png" width="440" height="277" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
            <info>
               <p>This ensures that the correct lookup will be returned to the record. To remove an existing Online Lookup, click<b>Remove</b>.

</p>
            <fig>
                     <title>98668077</title>
                     <image href="../attachments/98667726/98668077.png" placement="break" width="440" height="277">
                        <alt>placeholder</alt>
                     </image>
                  </fig></info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click <b>Close</b>.</cmd>
         </step>
      </steps>
   </taskbody>
</task>